attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a spine.** Columns 0 to 3, `gabT` to `glaH`, are carried by 95 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 1% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 99% of them, and no column of this stretch hesitates more than 0.19 bits {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at columns 4 and 5**, carried by 54 to 66%, the stretch most in regions of plasticity, 59% {S2, P}. Then a spine of 14 columns, 6 to 19, `smpB` to `rplS`, carried by 91 to 93%, [[ribosome maturation and translation]] {S3, Q}. Through columns 49 to 51, `rseA` to `rseC`, a group runs, [[sigma factor regulation]] {S4.c45-71, Q}.

@model **Here the model names fewer genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 83 against 89%, and hesitates more there, 0.88 against 0.57 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 4, is a fork column, at 4.51 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on variable columns and forks.** Columns 73 to 77, `glyA` to `yphE`, are carried by 3 to 50%, all persistent {S4.c73-77}. The last column is `yphC`, in 39% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 88% of genes**, 0.64 bits on average, perplexity 2.0 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 2.17 against 0.20 bits, and names fewer genes, 52% against 98% {C}.

